{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Seven days you shall celebrate.</b> Since on Pesah you were preoccupied with the barley harvest, and on Shavuot with the wheat harvest, I did not burden you except one day. But on the festival of Sukkot, when everything is gathered indoors and you have no preoccupation at all, you must celebrate seven days. Another interpretation: because you have much expenditure in it — gathering everything into the house and also setting aside second tithe — you celebrate seven days, unlike Pesah and Atzeret. Another interpretation: because each and every day is a festival in itself, since it is distinct in its offerings." "<b>Seven days you shall celebrate.</b> Unlike Pesah. But Shemini Atzeret need not be mentioned explicitly — presumably, when one goes up on pilgrimage for the festival of Sukkot there, Shemini is included, since when those depart it enters. And for this reason Scripture did not mention it either in the portion of Mishpatim and in the portion of Tissa, but in the portion of Emor and in the portion of Pinchas, which deal with offerings, it mentioned them explicitly, since the offerings are distinct." "<b>And you shall be altogether joyful.</b> Rashi explains, and according to his Talmud we learn from here to include the nights of the last festival day for rejoicing — that is, from <b>and you shall be altogether joyful</b>, to include it together with the seven days preceding it. For <b>אך</b> here comes to divide, to include the night of the last festival day, which has rejoicing before it, as is stated in the chapter of Lulav and Aravah. And according to its plain sense: <b>and you shall be altogether joyful</b> — that all your fruits are gathered into the house and into the storehouse, unlike Pesah and Shavuot; and therefore it is written regarding Pesah, 'and you shall turn in the morning,' etc., even though its duration is seven days."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:08.907418028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}